diff --git a/SHARED-CACHE.md b/SHARED-CACHE.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..730586e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/SHARED-CACHE.md
@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@
+# Shared cache directory (patched Nx)
+
+This Nx carries the shared-cache repair from `patches/nx@23.2.1.patch` (smoothbricks/codebase). Its presence is how a
+tool that prepares a cache directory for several checkouts tells that this Nx can share one.
+
+A cache directory holding a `.shared` file is shared by checkouts that each keep their own task database
+(`workspace-data`). In such a directory:
+
+- An entry is `<hash>/` (the task's outputs) plus `terminalOutputs/<hash>`, as in every Nx cache.
+- An entry is **published** once `<hash>.complete` exists. It holds the task's exit code and is renamed into place
+  after the outputs and terminal output are complete. A published entry is never rewritten.
+- A writer holds `<hash>.lock` (created with `O_EXCL`) while it stores an entry. A hash that is locked or already
+  published is left to its writer; a lock older than ten minutes belongs to a writer that died and is taken over.
+- A checkout whose own database has no row for a hash adopts a published entry: it records the row and restores the
+  entry like any local hit. A row whose `<hash>/` is gone is a miss, never a hit that restores nothing.
+- Nx neither bounds nor ages the directory: each checkout's rows age on their own, so its bound would delete entries
+  other checkouts still name. The directory's owner prunes it, removing `<hash>.complete` before `<hash>/`.
